--TEST--
`$_` written where no `|>` encloses it names nothing and is refused — `rule:expressions/pipeline-hole-once`'s E0131
--FILE--
<?nvs
// rule:expressions/pipeline-hole-once — `$_` is a hole and never a variable,
// so outside a right side the fix is a `|>` and not a declaration.
echo $_, "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0131]: `$_` is the pipeline hole and has no meaning here
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
